{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/448843-selling-my-players-on-demon","id":448843,"title":"Selling my players on Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-18T22:22:17-07:00","id":448843,"title":"Selling my players on Demon","content":"firstly I have game ADD, and we're currently playing HtV, but eventually I'd like to run a Demon game with my players, but they don't seem interested, though I'm not sure why. I think maybe I'm not explaining it well... or they're having trouble associating it with familiar fiction.<br /> <br /> Suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 03-19-2015, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T22:35:54-07:00","id":448866,"title":"","content":"How did you describe it to your players? Did they say any of it in particular sounded uninteresting or unappealing? What are the kinds of things they usually like?<br /> <br /> I can sympathize with distractibility. I find I generally get more enjoyment from sticking with one game for a longer haul, though, even if there are other games whose concepts I'd like better. It's hard enough to make a game stick, but it's rewarding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T04:22:13-07:00","id":448996,"title":"","content":"I don't know your players, but I can think of a few general approaches.<br /> <br /> The Awesome Powers approach. As a demon you're incredibly powerful. Perfect multilingual liars, amazingly good at masquerading as human, with powers that include manipulation of causality, time travel, the ability to shoot fire, have detachable limbs, reveal addition limbs, have a built-in arm cannon... Murder By Improbability pretty much gives them a death note, if they're anime fans. You get to design your cool demonic form and the powers that make it tick. You get unique, custom powers in the form of Interlocks. You can install your powers into gadgets, tweaking their effects as you do so. Do your players like making their own powers? Do they like being powerful? Demon's got you covered.<br /> <br /> The Science Fiction approach. The Matrix, Sapphire and Steel, Dark City... All of these can be considered inspirational sources for demon. If your players like science fiction, especially anything cyberpunky, you cab get a lot of mileage out of this pitch. Demon is the most sci-fi of the World of Darkness games. You can play as living glitches, cyborg spies and weirder things.<br /> <br /> The Spy Fiction approach. Any of your players fans of the Bourne films? Or books? Anything Cold War related? The less cheesy Bond films? The cheesy Bond films? Demon's an espionage game where you thwart monolithic, institutional evil, where you can never be certain who your friends are and you're one wrong move away from a tense chase scene as hunter angels converge on you. Your players will be hacking mainframes, pulling heists, hits, protecting witnesses and uncovering terrible truths. They can be Q Branch, installing Combustion into a pen and building extradimensional spaces into their cars. They can be impossible gunmen, superspies who knock enemies out with a single punch. Or they can be desperate men, their array of powers and tricks the slim hope that keeps them from being overwhelmed by the God-Machine's angels, the temptation to defect (and the paranoia that your allies already have) wearing them down every day.<br /> <br /> There's also a Conspiracy Theorist approach that kinda overlaps the two above.<br /> <br /> The Demon approach. You're demons who rebelled against God, a God that isn't benign, though Its ultimate aim is unknown and probably unknowable, and could conceivably be malign or even completely insane. You've stumbled upon free will and humanity. What you do with that is up to you. Reign in hell? Start a war against God? All viable. You can aim to supplant God, to forge a literal hell, Biblical or otherwise, <br /> <br /> With distractable players, and if you yourself find it hard to stick, perhaps offer a one-shot Demon game.If your players like it you can casually offer to make it the next main game. if not, you tried and hopefully scratched your demonic itch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T05:55:37-07:00","id":449053,"title":"","content":"They might be turned off by the whole techno-espionage angle. I know that, when I play the WoD, I want to sit down and play a monster, not something out of Shadowrun or the Matrix. If I wanted to play Shadowrun, I would actually play Shadowrun. <br /> <br /> But here's why I like Demon. Because I don't see it as techno-espionage. I see Fallen Angels waging the eternal war against the Hosts of Angels. Religion has it wrong. Demons didn't all fall with Satan, and Michael didn't cast them all into Hell. That war? It never ended. <br /> <br /> Messengers? They're your succubi and incubi; while they're not all vampy and draining your life or dreams, they're definitely the tempters who lure you into falling away from God. <br /> Guardians? They're the Grigori, the Watcher Angels who fell when they found mortals fair. Or, in some cases, too foul to let live.<br /> Psychopomps? <a href=\"http://fc04.deviantart.net/fs70/i/2009/341/e/1/Buer_by_DarkSky666.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Well, they're the crazy, inhuman ones, like this one.</a><br /> Destroyers? Affinity for fire and red skin, animal parts? They're such the classical horned devil, its not even funny.<br /> Analysts? They're imps! Its right there, in the reasons for falling!<br /> <br /> I could go into more, but I think this highlights what I'm trying to get at. The book conveys a lot of high tech machine-theme, but when you play the game, there's a lot of more of the classical demony feel to the game that you think at first glance. Infrastructure is an &quot;holy&quot; ritual that you have to stop or subborn, twist to your own ends. Example angels include literal beings of light that can only be hurt by weapons forged in absolute darkness. The comparisons go on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:17:24-07:00","id":449286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/448843-selling-my-players-on-demon?p=448866#post448866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can sympathize with distractibility. I find I generally get more enjoyment from sticking with one game for a longer haul, though, even if there are other games whose concepts I'd like better. It's hard enough to make a game stick, but it's rewarding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon is very much that new shiny, and I think I empathize with it a lot, I personally see a lot of concepts that fit with programming. I killed our werewolf game because I realized I couldn't empathize with it enough to tell a story in it. I killed a previous game because well... the characters weren't seeming to form a coherent unit and mixed Super game is a bad idea ...in this context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/448843-selling-my-players-on-demon?p=448866#post448866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did you describe it to your players?</div> </div> </div> </div> I've jumped around to different aspects like spy's and god machine like skynet, and some of the cool powers demons have (e.g. equating deep pockets to the scene in the Mask where they pull a bazooka out of his pocket, which at least one of them immediately came up with the room of weapons idea).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/448843-selling-my-players-on-demon?p=448866#post448866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they say any of it in particular sounded uninteresting or unappealing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly no though, I think the espionage thing may be less appealing.<br /> <br /> I think also any attempt by me to explain the God Machine or what it's like being these things fails, because of my programming perspective, I'm the only programmer, so none of that is going to make sense to them, e.g. deep pockets could work because if you know the location of something in memory you can make a pointer to it, presuming that a security check won't stop you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/448843-selling-my-players-on-demon?p=448866#post448866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the kinds of things they usually like?</div> </div> </div> </div>They seem to be a little more of &quot;smash&quot; and &quot;pulp&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:09:31-07:00","id":449438,"title":"","content":"Set up a one shot with them as a ring of sabatoures. They have just been given information about a critical piece of infrastructure. The location, the access points and a general idea of security but no specific details on construction or purpose.<br /> <br /> Folded space complex that is hidden in a closet of an abandoned warehouse. <br /> <br /> If you want to show them the system in a simple form give them a one shot that is a smash and dash. In my opinion with this one shot you show don't tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T12:21:45-07:00","id":449572,"title":"","content":"Watch some episodes of Burn Notice with them. Great for getting into the spy mood while still communicating that you could be using homemade bombs or tumbling over cars in the street.<br /> <br /> Forget the machine metaphor, then; go with the society metaphor and secret occult laws. God is the scale of modern society. God is something alien built into our governments and our corporations and the very infrastructure we power cities with. You were part of God, just another expendable agent, until you decided you weren't so expendable anymore. You found something else in the human life you were sent out into that you valued more, and you rebelled. Now, you are what is standing between the omnipresent enemy, the cold and sterile holy presence, and the things you care about. You have faces to wear. They are all you. None of them are you. And when your back is against the wall, you will unfold your final face, and as molten glass rains from the sky at your behest, you will show God that you have improved on his lessons.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, tell 'em about going loud and demonic forms. Those are punchy and direct.<br /> <br /> And if they're still not hooked, that's okay. One size doesn't fit all; it just doesn't fit their preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T12:54:22-07:00","id":449622,"title":"","content":"Have you dropped Matrix references? Because rogue Matrix agents is a decent start to defining some cool aspects. It is something of a lie to children, but can give some context and is closer then Baphomet, Baal, and the Hellzapoppin gang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}